        "original_id": "a3708936-ea5e-5e97-b668-09414a33d40e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Patrick Carpentier\n- Organizations: NASCAR Sprint Cup Series, Go FAS Racing, CART\n- Products: Ford Fusion, Lincoln MKZ, Mercury Milan, CD3 platform\n- Events: 1997 CART season, 1997 Marlboro 500\n- Places: Ford Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant\n\nFacts:\n- Patrick Carpentier was born on August 13, 1971, and he is a Canadian professional auto racing driver.\n- Patrick Carpentier was the Rookie of the Year in the 1997 CART season.\n- The 1997 Marlboro 500 was the 17th and final round of the 1997 CART season.\n- For the 2006 model year, Ford introduced the Fusion.\n- The Ford Fusion is manufactured at Ford's Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant alongside the Lincoln MKZ, and it was formerly built there with the discontinued Mercury Milan; all three shared the CD3 platform.\n- Patrick Carpentier competed part-time in the NASCAR Sprint Cup Series, driving the No. 32 Ford Fusion for Go FAS Racing.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
